From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xinyang <xinyang@localhost>
Date: Sun, 16 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: preserve timestamps on error buffers (7.3.4)

Iris clears the timestamp when returning a buffer with V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR,
even when firmware supplied a valid timestamp. With a corrupted HEVC frame
on HFI gen2, firmware returns the frame with HFI_INFO_DATA_CORRUPT and its
original timestamp, but userspace receives an empty error buffer with
timestamp zero. This prevents clients such as libva-v4l2 from identifying
the failed picture and can leave them waiting for it until a synchronization
timeout.

Copy the recorded timestamp to error buffers so userspace can associate the
error with the corresponding input. Keep the error state and zero payload
unchanged; this does not assume that the corrupted image is suitable for
display.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
index eb8de60c1..f790483d1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
@@ -899,7 +899,8 @@ int iris_vb2_buffer_done(struct iris_inst *inst, struct iris_buffer *buf)
 	if (buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR) {
 		state = VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR;
 		vb2_set_plane_payload(vb2, 0, 0);
-		vb2->timestamp = 0;
+		/* Allow userspace to associate the error with the input frame. */
+		vb2->timestamp = buf->timestamp;
 		v4l2_m2m_buf_done(vbuf, state);
 		return 0;
 	}

